============================================================
Sitewide axe result
============================================================
FAIL. The worker's own probe (which I also ran unmodified and got a clean
result from) has an incomplete reveal set: it never opens the /whatif
results-tab workspace ([data-wf-tab]/[data-wf-panel], 4 of 5 tabs), never
types into a search box, and never clicks a toggle lacking
aria-expanded. Exercising those three ordinary, real interaction paths
turns up 3 distinct, axe-confirmed violations (all in the wcag2a/2aa/22aa
ruleset the worker itself scoped to) on 2 of the 9 pages named in
criterion (d). The underlying markup for all three predates this task
(git diff master is byte-identical for the failing classes/structure),
but U15's acceptance criterion (d) is explicitly "axe zero violations
sitewide, both themes" as the FINAL a11y sweep for this whole run — that
is this task's entire reason for existing, not an incidental side-effect
of unrelated work, so a real violation surviving it is a FAIL of this
task's own stated deliverable, reported with full provenance above.

============================================================
OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking, for the backlog)
============================================================
- /filemanager "Setup" nav-group color-contrast: reproduces ONLY at
  ~1024px (nav wraps); absent at 390/1280/1440. Confirmed independently.
  Correctly flagged by the worker as backlog, not a U15 defect.
- The `axe_probe.js` reveal-selector gap (no [data-wf-tab] handling, no
  search-box-typing simulation, no generic "click every disclosure that
  lacks aria-expanded" fallback) is itself worth promoting to a permanent
  fixture of the sitewide oracle for future runs, not just a one-off
  fix for Quick Adjust — the same blind spot class recurred twice in this
  task alone.
- healthcare-card.html's "+ Add Person" form is the ONLY
  `data-toggle-add-*`-without-`aria-expanded` disclosure in the app;
  giving it `aria-expanded` (matching the settings-rail convention
  elsewhere) would both fix the semantic gap and make it visible to the
  existing reveal script's `[aria-expanded="false"]` selector.
